; Co-recursion carrier (session-21 P6.1): two MUTUALLY recursive relations
; `ping` and `pong` form ONE strongly-connected component (ping from pong,
; pong from ping). The regional model's `recursive-component` block must group
; them as ONE component members=(ping, pong) spanning the cycle: a size-2
; members list is the co-recursion signal, distinct from tc's size-1
; self-recursion. There is NO `#query`; recursion detection runs off the
; DataFlow SCC condensation (Stratify), which is query-independent. Results are
; observed through the published `reachable_pair` message.
#message add_edge(u64 From, u64 To).
#message reachable_pair(u64 From, u64 To).

#local ping(u64 A, u64 B).
#local pong(u64 A, u64 B).

ping(A, B) : add_edge(A, B).
pong(A, B) : ping(A, B).
ping(A, B) : pong(A, X), add_edge(X, B).

reachable_pair(A, B) : ping(A, B).
